[
    {
        "content": "<p>If I try this on Lean playground latest Mathlib</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>then it fails but if I select Mathlib stable or Mathlib v4.28.0 then it succeeds</p>",
        "id": 587801971,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1776700177
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Both <code>NormedAddCommGroup G</code> and <code>LieRing G</code> contain <code>AddCommGroup G</code>, so you added two separate addition operations on <code>G</code>.</p>",
        "id": 587810322,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776702294
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SeminormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- synth before `LieRing`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- synth after `LieRing`</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 587810618,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776702383
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So are you saying 4.28 and Mathlib stable should have produced errors but did not?</p>",
        "id": 587810683,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1776702409
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38126\">#38126</a> (overlapping instances linter) would probably flag this, but it's still being worked on</p>",
        "id": 587810881,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776702455
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>idk why the behavior changed, but regardless I think this is incorrect code. You need some way of defining both structures together, e.g. <code>[LieRing G] [IsNormed G]</code> (I made these up)</p>",
        "id": 587811179,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776702533
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am too used to Haskell - and as soon as I saw overlapping instances that would have been a red flag that I had gone wrong - well more power to the overlapping instances linter then - many thanks</p>",
        "id": 587812561,
        "sender_full_name": "Dominic Steinitz",
        "timestamp": 1776702958
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure about this but I think that <code>extends</code> automagically unifies overlapping instances, so a possible solution would be to define your own class:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedLieRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LieRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedLieRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 587813165,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776703153
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110050\">@Sébastien Gouëzel</span> this is one of the disadvantages of not extracting the norm hierarchy, right? </p>\n<p>Right now Mathlib has <code>NormedRing</code>, <code>NormedGroup</code>, <code>NormedField</code>, <code>NormedAlgebra</code>, <code>NormedAddGroup</code>, <code>NormedAddCommGroup</code>, <code>NormedCommRing</code>, <code>NormedCommGroup</code>, <code>NormedStarGroup</code> and Snir's approach does indeed conform with our current design decisions. These decisions have been discussed extensively; the alternative, making a <code>HasNorm</code> class and then turning all of these classes into (fewer) predicates such as <code>IsNormedRing</code>, <code>IsNormedGroup</code>, <code>IsNormedAddgroup</code> unfortunately has other disadvantages (for example, more <code>variable</code>s) and right now, after several experiments, we have decided to leave things as they are.</p>\n<p>If you decide to go down this route then look at how e.g. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=NormedAddCommGroup#doc\">docs#NormedAddCommGroup</a> is defined and mimic that.</p>",
        "id": 587818852,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1776704953
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there an axiom relating the Lie bracket and the norm?</p>",
        "id": 587820051,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1776705342
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks very much everyone - what I should have written was something like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">HG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HG</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ModelWithCorners</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HG</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LieAlgebraValuedOneForm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">letI</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">EG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Cₛ</span><span class=\"bp\">^∞⟮</span><span class=\"n\">IP</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GroupLieAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GroupLieAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IG</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"bp\">⟯</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
